Egyptian prototypes and that the use of the butterfly motif argues against the 
artifact’s [...] The study proposes that the platform depicted in the ring is 
supported by incurved altars, mirroring construction styles revealed by the 
Xeste 3 fresco, unknown to scholars until the 1970s.\n\nWhen was the ring of 
Nestor first published and what was its initial reception?add\n\nPublished in 
